{
  "core_message": "A bear eating a lost drug drop became a real 1985 murder mystery.",
  "mood": "curious",
  "title": "Cocaine‑Fueled Bear Rampage: The 1985 Georgia Murder Puzzle",
  "description": "In 1985, a pilot dropped a bag of cocaine in a Georgia forest and died hitting the doorframe. A black bear ate the drugs, became violent, and one hiker never came home.\n\nThe police found the bear's stomach full of cocaine. The case never got solved, but it became a legend.\n\nBased on the Wikipedia article \"Cocaine Bear\" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cocaine_Bear), licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.\n\nImages from Wikimedia Commons:\nDiscovery Channel comes to the Defense Language Institute Foreign Language Center at the Presidio of Monterey, California on 10 January 2008 - 4.jpg (Presidio of Monterey: DLIFLC &amp; USAG, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Discovery_Channel_comes_to_the_Defense_Language_Institute_Foreign_Language_Center_at_the_Presidio_of_Monterey,_California_on_10_January_2008_-_4.jpg\nDiscovery Channel comes to the Defense Language Institute Foreign Language Center at the Presidio of Monterey, California on 10 January 2008 - 1.jpg (Presidio of Monterey: DLIFLC &amp; USAG, Public domain): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Discovery_Channel_comes_to_the_Defense_Language_Institute_Foreign_Language_Center_at_the_Presidio_of_Monterey,_California_on_10_January_2008_-_1.jpg",
